**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 

**How to implement.** A pulled version says which bytes of its record it was built from, so that updating a source can mint a version only where the record changed (001 §D 'Updating a source mints a NEW version when the record changed and never mutates one'; the S13.1 brief 'mints a NEW version only where a record's hash changed'; 001 §B 'Identity is GUID + version + hash'). The hash rides in the provenance, so the entry file, the database payload and a kit's snapshot of a pulled version all carry it (001 §C 'Hybrid shape'), and the library database's model and its schema stamp stay as they are (`LibraryDatabaseStore.fs`, step 62: `LibrarySchemaVersion.current` stays 1). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S13.1. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryEntryFiles.fs`: `SourcePullInfo` (step 24) gains `recordHash : ContentHash` directly after `record`: the SHA-256 of the record's text as the source's snapshot held it when this version was pulled, computed by `ContentHash.ofBytes` (step 123). Its field doc is one line. No other provenance case, member or field changes; `attributionOpt` (step 113), `protection` and `categoryOrigin` (step 24) read no hash. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/schema/library-common.schema.json` (steps 30, 91, 405): the pulled-from-source provenance shape gains the required key `recordHash`, referencing the content-hash definition the file already holds (`^[0-9a-f]{64}$`, step 30), so a pulled provenance without it fails the schema. The entry schemas keep version 1, because no entry file holding a pulled provenance has been released (.spec-md §7; step 405's precedent). (3) Every construction of a `SourcePullInfo` sets the field, and no assertion changes: `OpticalConstructor.Tests/BuiltinCatalogue.fs`' `licensedMaterialContent` (step 113) sets `recordHash = ContentHash.ofBytes (Encoding.UTF8.GetBytes "test/<name>")`, the hash of its record id's text; the literals of `LibraryEntryFilesTests.fs` and `EntryFileJsonTests.fs` (steps 24, 30, 91, 113, 405) each set `ContentHash.ofBytes` of a test-local text. (4) Tests. `EntryFileJsonTests` gains `a pulled provenance keeps its record's hash through an entry file, and a file without it is refused`: a material under `SourcePullProvenance` whose `recordHash` is `ContentHash.ofBytes` of the UTF-8 bytes of `abc` (`ContentHash "ba7816bf8f01cfea414140de5dae2223b00361a396177a9cb410ff61f20015ad"`, step 123) round-trips content → `sealed` → `fileText` → `parseEntry` (step 30), its decoded provenance holding that hash; the same file text with the `recordHash` key removed answers `SchemaValidationErr`. `every provenance round-trips through an entry file` and `a pulled entry and its forks carry its licence's attribution, and every other provenance none` keep their assertions.

**Acceptance.** After the record hash lands, `SourcePullInfo` MUST carry `recordHash : ContentHash` and `library-common.schema.json` MUST require it for a pulled provenance, with no change to the library database's model or schema stamp; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a pulled provenance keeps its record's hash through an entry file, and a file without it is refused` and the unchanged `every provenance round-trips through an entry file` and `a pulled entry and its forks carry its licence's attribution, and every other provenance none`, the count rising by 1; and build, elevation and the twenty-one s43 invariants MUST pass.
